{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_3b8355bc5017ac70fa08cf5c29fe3b69fc3c4030b40832ab0d959edf0f488e8e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The terminal UI uses a Catppuccin Mocha role-mapped palette with Catppuccin Blue as the sole accent, status colors mapped one-to-one to orchestrator session statuses, and Unicode-only iconography with no emoji."}],"claim_ids":["clm_3b8355bc5017ac70fa08cf5c29fe3b69fc3c4030b40832ab0d959edf0f488e8e"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:05:36Z","created_by_operation":"op_727ce1c0c25c4a01934302190a6fcebc","id":"pg_88932296c6165b128b764fa7d0a1c0d4","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/bastani-inc-atomic-design-md-ca64fa07885f-4fa7d0a1c0d4.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_33a6f061b716592a96f00a65a03e696a"],"title":"bastani-inc/atomic/DESIGN.md @ ca64fa07885f","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:05:36Z","updated_by_operation":"op_727ce1c0c25c4a01934302190a6fcebc"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:05:36Z","created_by_operation":"op_727ce1c0c25c4a01934302190a6fcebc","id":"pg_de4f272d5fa65cd1be3daa8b44ccc954","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/bastani-inc-atomic-product-md-ca64fa07885f-aa8b44ccc954.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_3a662ed25038509f9591ec84f8786c13"],"title":"bastani-inc/atomic/PRODUCT.md @ ca64fa07885f","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:05:36Z","updated_by_operation":"op_727ce1c0c25c4a01934302190a6fcebc"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_1aa62b3f9bf573abec8aaa02356bec1f8463366f73aac39a829e198d15b6c490"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Atomic implements the Agent Skills standard and can use configured Claude Code or Codex skill directories without rewriting them; skills can be auto-selected from descriptions or invoked with /skill:<name>."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3ed2955cbcbfe13de480288197471e8a07f4f1b57883a3b3367d18588f7f5676"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Atomic is a fork of Pi and works with providers, tools, MCP servers, skills, and extensions from an existing Pi stack; it connects to model providers directly rather than wrapping other coding tools."},{"claim_ids":["clm_414978fb23471071bb022d4cf608c86ee6867ee13e6ad9a60d81d0ca52c71f69"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Workflows persist artifacts such as plans, logs, transcripts, reviewer notes, check output, and summaries; research commonly lives in research/ and specs in specs/."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4ae536c8d4bfc6d3685b31f4c3e160a2720366ec7111e1f4906e8089e5fe2a13"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The Linux musl release archives bundle their C++ runtime and run on stock Alpine, but Android and Termux are unsupported; provider availability depends on credentials, subscription, region, and the provider catalog."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4f8d76953140fdfd7d146670d8c5e9dd2a9c28a6595be59bc45bb0036bcc6a23"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Stages can prompt an agent, run tools, call MCP servers, save artifacts, branch, retry, run in parallel, or pause for approval; specialized subagents handle focused work while a parent agent or workflow controls the larger task."},{"claim_ids":["clm_55718a22ece9d6a122c394ad39ed3fdc21cdd4afca19a238bc2dde8da0525145"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI exposes workflow management commands including /workflow list, inputs, status, connect, quit, and resume; quitting pauses a run so it can resume later."},{"claim_ids":["clm_754d00b01ed591828812e41971dfb6f30ace674d7ad6e0e7691abc9118ef4d82"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Atomic ships three top-level building blocks: workflows, skills, and specialized subagents, with nine bundled subagent definitions such as worker, debugger, and codebase-analyzer."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7f35ecc6278348c7f94936dc04ee74c2e91852fbd716819ceb6918d9e18075db"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Non-interactive use is supported via atomic -p \"<prompt>\", which prints the response and exits; provider credentials are stored in ~/.atomic/agent/auth.json with owner-only permissions where the platform supports them."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8b6d78c7883d39f4daaed1ea64c035cbcc03b56b98af96984f64eee318396bd2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Package installation requires Node.js 22.19 or newer plus npm, pnpm, Yarn, or Bun (Bun 1.4.2+ for Bun installs); a self-contained release archive path needs no Node.js or package manager."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c6de7e1d48e5a0b82ad01433fe0a14b228ae2cee14bd2f607cafe5a17e4e34cb"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Workflows are authored as TypeScript workflow({...}) definitions whose stage dependencies must form a directed acyclic graph; cyclic graphs are unsupported, and loop/repair iterations must create distinct tracked work per iteration."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e4867eaf18a8eb7ef33839806768004447c1628fc545d196f5445953c2c808d4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Atomic has no built-in sandbox or command-level shell permission gate; tools and extensions run with the user's permissions, and the README recommends running autonomous work in a devcontainer, VM, or remote machine."}],"claim_ids":["clm_1aa62b3f9bf573abec8aaa02356bec1f8463366f73aac39a829e198d15b6c490","clm_3ed2955cbcbfe13de480288197471e8a07f4f1b57883a3b3367d18588f7f5676","clm_414978fb23471071bb022d4cf608c86ee6867ee13e6ad9a60d81d0ca52c71f69","clm_4ae536c8d4bfc6d3685b31f4c3e160a2720366ec7111e1f4906e8089e5fe2a13","clm_4f8d76953140fdfd7d146670d8c5e9dd2a9c28a6595be59bc45bb0036bcc6a23","clm_55718a22ece9d6a122c394ad39ed3fdc21cdd4afca19a238bc2dde8da0525145","clm_754d00b01ed591828812e41971dfb6f30ace674d7ad6e0e7691abc9118ef4d82","clm_7f35ecc6278348c7f94936dc04ee74c2e91852fbd716819ceb6918d9e18075db","clm_8b6d78c7883d39f4daaed1ea64c035cbcc03b56b98af96984f64eee318396bd2","clm_c6de7e1d48e5a0b82ad01433fe0a14b228ae2cee14bd2f607cafe5a17e4e34cb","clm_e4867eaf18a8eb7ef33839806768004447c1628fc545d196f5445953c2c808d4"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:05:36Z","created_by_operation":"op_727ce1c0c25c4a01934302190a6fcebc","id":"pg_f935c052b21a5b0b8a5c4e3aecbc1c9b","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/bastani-inc-atomic-readme-md-ca64fa07885f-4e3aecbc1c9b.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_a79e9df099a05d4196058e640a174b9b"],"title":"bastani-inc/atomic/README.md @ ca64fa07885f","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:05:36Z","updated_by_operation":"op_727ce1c0c25c4a01934302190a6fcebc"}
